From 3b614784d3146c5cc0dfba05247c7037c528b081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tad <tad.keller@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:43:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] libcamera: software_isp: debayer_cpu: Add NV12 output

The CPU debayer only produces RGB formats. The Android camera HAL needs
a YUV 4:2:0 stream (NV12 or NV21) for the mandatory YCbCr_420_888 and
IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED formats, and as the source of its JPEG encoder,
so cameras behind the software ISP are rejected by the HAL.

Add NV12 output. Each line pair is debayered to RGB888 scratch lines
with the existing functions (so black level, gains, CCM and gamma all
apply), then converted to two Y lines and one interleaved CbCr line,
chroma averaged over 2x2 pixels. The conversion is full-range BT.601
(JFIF), matching the sYCC colour space the simple pipeline reports for
YUV output.

The UV plane is taken from the second plane of the output buffer, or
from after the Y plane when the buffer has a single plane (as buffers
exported by the software ISP do). Only Bayer patterns of height 2 are
supported, which covers all current input formats.
